fluorine-desktop (0.9.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add flr-settings, a native GTK4 and libadwaita control panel with a
    two-pane navigation layout and six sections: Appearance, Workstation,
    Displays, Network and Bluetooth, Audio, and System and Snapshots.
  * Every control delegates to an existing flr-* command, so the panel and the
    keyboard workflow read and write the same state: flr-wall for wallpapers,
    flr-shader for the display shader, flr-mode for the workstation profile,
    flr-snapshot for the snapshot list, and wpctl for default sink and source
    volume.
  * Add flr-config, which keeps the editable geometry and idle state in
    ~/.config/fluorine/config.lua and applies it to the Hyprland gaps and
    border width plus the hyprlock listener in hypridle.conf.
  * Ship a desktop entry so the panel appears in Fuzzel, bind SUPER + comma to
    flr-settings, add Settings as the first flr-ctl entry, and open the panel
    as an 880x600 centred floating window.
  * Apply config.lua at session start so the saved geometry and idle timeout
    survive a restart.

 -- gowthvm <gowthamgkofficial@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:05:00 +0530

fluorine-desktop (0.8.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add flr-wall, a wallpaper switcher that lists the shipped 4K set in
    /usr/share/backgrounds/fluorine and any image in ~/Pictures/Wallpapers,
    applies a choice through swaybg, and remembers it in
    ~/.local/state/fluorine/wallpaper.
  * Keep the lock screen in step by rewriting the hyprlock background path
    whenever the wallpaper changes, and restore the saved wallpaper from the
    Hyprland start hook instead of starting swaybg with a bare color.
  * Bind SUPER + W to the Fuzzel wallpaper picker and add a Wallpaper entry to
    the flr-ctl system menu.

 -- gowthvm <gowthamgkofficial@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:10:00 +0530

fluorine-desktop (0.7.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Calibrate window geometry and motion: 4px corner rounding, a short
    monochrome black shadow so stacked windows stay legible on dark wallpapers,
    and two bounded cubic-bezier curves that drive 150-200ms window, fade,
    layer, and workspace animations with no overshoot or spring bounce.
  * Blur Waybar, Fuzzel, and both SwayNC layer surfaces with ignore_alpha set to
    zero, so transparent panel pixels stay unblurred and text contrast is
    untouched.
  * Align Waybar, Fuzzel, and SwayNC on one surface language: 32px carbon bar
    with a hairline bottom border, lime underline instead of lime fill for the
    active workspace, 8px internal padding everywhere, and matching 1.5px
    hairline borders on panels, cards, and tooltips.
  * Add flr-shader, which switches decoration:screen_shader between the
    color-accurate default, a warm night pass, and a grayscale focus mode,
    remembers the choice, restores it at login, and is bound to SUPER + Shift +
    N and listed in the flr-ctl system menu.

 -- gowthvm <gowthamgkofficial@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:10:00 +0530

